  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Roman Alcocer. I work in clinical operations compliance — the part of drug development
    that makes sure trials are run the way they're supposed to be — and I live in Oakland, California.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before that I did document control and clinical quality at a small psychedelics nonprofit, and
    I studied math as an undergrad, most of which I've forgotten and some of which I'm trying to get back.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site exists so there's one place on the internet that's mine: essays when I have them, a
    log of the books I've read, and whatever else earns a page.
  </p>

